d":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"NYiL2534CAAbr-ynGVbhaQ","review_id":"LkD2ljn9tu5TPzTzYuDhDg","date":"2019-05-01T16:35:17","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9421374797821045,"text_excerpt":"My wife and I loved our experience at Cafe Sbisa. Definitely a classy, fine place to enjoy some New Orleans food and perhaps even some light jazz if you're lucky. We were fortunate to find a table for 2 with no reservations on a Friday evening. We found the place very romantic and quaint and didn't plan to come here--only ended up after a nearby spot had a two hour wait. I do recommend you make reservations if you come here as I feel like we got lucky. We were seated upstairs and started with the turtle soup and gumbo. The turtle soup had a nice spice kick while the gumbo had a strong seafood flavor. Both were spectacular and the garlic bread that kept coming was sooo fantastic, fluffy, g..."},{"business_id":"NYiL2534CAAbr-ynGVbhaQ","review_id":"66f-HykzGX3rwveFs-04hw","date":"2019-09-02T00:35:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9392551183700562,"text_excerpt":"I am writing this review as I still sit at the table. This place is AMAZING. Service, food, ambiance, it is absolutely PERFECT! You will not be disappointed. Come for a nice dinner or date night feel. The best meal and experience we had in NOLA for our anniversary trip. My husband got the gumbo, which was chicken and sausage that night. AMAZING. (We went to Commander's palace the night before, and their gumbo was not good. It was like gravy.) I got the Wedge salad with the garlic Parmesan dressing. AMAZING. Our entrees? My husband got the rack of lamb, and I got the trout Eugene. Both so delicious. I'm not a lamb person so I can't speak on that, but it was played beautifully. My husband l..."},{"business_id":"NYiL2534CAAbr-ynGVbhaQ","review_id":"_Yd6Xs0n96prz62BIJ3PAA","date":"2017-09-18T01:20:39","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9368093013763428,"text_excerpt":"Update! Had my birthday dinner here on August 17th! Food is five star. Let me start with the crab cakes: they are the best I've ever had. Just wow. Crispy, well balanced, and unbelievably flavorful. I got the catch of the day which is all locals and added fixings of crab meat. Unlike tourist restaurants, cafe sbisa does New Orleans classics in a refined, attention to detail manner. Great place to bring friends or family visiting from out of town! They'll get the Nola vibe and cuisine they want without the poor service and soggy food of the tourist spots. I was so impressed with the service. Everyone was so kind and knowledgeable, and a sweet girl offered to take my boyfriend's and my pict..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"NYiL2534CAAbr-ynGVbhaQ","photo_id":"8TYcK6MWjmVCrxIvVUpPBg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/8TYcK6MWjmVCrxIvVUpPBg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9104738235473633},{"business_id":"NYiL2534CAAbr-ynGVbhaQ","photo_id